@page "/docs/dialog-service"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.DialogService
<PageTitle>Dialog Service - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Dialog Service</h1>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Secondary">imperative</BzBadge>
            <BzBadge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline">awaitable results</BzBadge>
        </div>
        <p>Open a confirmation, a prompt or any component from C# and <code>await</code> its result, with no markup or open state to wire up in the page. The service renders the same Dialog, AlertDialog and Sheet components you would write by hand, so focus trapping, scroll locking and animations behave exactly the same.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock SetupSnippet="DialogService/UsageSetup" Snippet="DialogService/Usage"
                Description="Register the service and the host once. After that, inject `IDialogService` wherever you need it and await a dialog from C#." />

    @* Setup and API are reference, not examples: plain code sections (no preview frame to leave
       empty) and h2s, so the TOC lists them beside Usage instead of nesting them under Examples. *@
    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Setup</h2>
        <p>Register the service once and add a single host at the root of your app.</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="DialogService/Setup" />
        <p>This docs app is already set up that way, with <code>AddBlaizio()</code> in <code>Program.cs</code> and one <code>&lt;DialogProvider /&gt;</code> in the layout, so every demo below is live.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">API</h2>
        <p>Inject <code>IDialogService</code> anywhere and call one of these methods:</p>
        <CodeBlock Snippet="DialogService/IDialogService" />
    </section>

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Confirmation" Description="The most common case: a yes or no question whose result is a `bool`."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceConfirmExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Destructive, custom labels" Description="Pass `BzDialogOptions` to change the button text and variant, for example a destructive confirm button."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceDestructiveExample)" />

    <Demo Title="A component as the dialog" Description="`ShowAsync<T>` shows any component as the dialog body. The component closes itself and hands back a typed value."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceComponentExample)" />

    <Demo Title="An inline template" Description="Pass a `RenderFragment` straight to `ShowAsync` when a separate component would be overkill. The template receives the dialog instance so it can close itself."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceTemplateExample)" />

    <Demo Title="A sheet instead of a window" Description="`ShowSheetAsync` shows the same content as a sheet that slides in from the edge you choose. `Start` and `End` are logical edges, so they mirror in right-to-left layouts, and the result is awaited the same way."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceSheetExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Stacking" Description="A confirm opened from inside an open dialog stacks on top of it. Focus trapping nests correctly, and the page stays scroll-locked until the last dialog closes."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceStackedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Locked while busy" Description="While a long operation runs, the component sets `Dialog.PreventDismiss` so Escape, the backdrop and the close button cannot dismiss it. When the work finishes, it closes itself."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceBusyExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization" Description="An inline template gives you full control of the dialog body, while the service still handles focus, scroll locking and the result. This example builds a branded upgrade prompt with a colored icon header."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceCustomizationExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL" Description="Service dialogs follow the app's direction, and a dialog body can also wrap itself in a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`. Here the header, text and footer buttons mirror."
          Example="typeof(DialogServiceRtlExample)" />

</div>

